    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score (81.88) against Ober. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from the 92% SB potential against a notoriously slow-moving pitcher, combined with a premium leadoff spot that maximizes his counting stats. Alongside him, **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.87) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) are elite starts; **Luis Robert Jr.** exploits a strong platoon advantage against P\u00e9rez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** finds a favorable park and solid SP matchup against Sandoval. **Jacob Wilson** (70.33) also jumps into the top tier, as his projected #3 spot and a soft matchup against Martinez make him a high-floor asset for today\u2019s 5x5 categories.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical, with **Nasim Nunez** (46.31) being the most difficult omission. While **Nasim Nunez** offers intrigue due to his switch-hitting profile and speed, the optimizer favored **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** for their superior projected production. **Jackson Merrill** (39.02) stayed on the bench as well, largely due to a difficult matchup against Harrison and the negative impact of an L/L platoon disadvantage, which keeps his efficiency below our 40-point threshold for active play.\n\nManagers must exercise caution regarding the 33% rain risk affecting **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Miguel Vargas** is a strong play (63.77) if the weather holds, the potential for a shortened game or delay presents a tangible risk to his counting stat accumulation. Furthermore, while we feel confident in our current projections, the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Liam Hicks**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages** means we must monitor official lineups closely; any shift out of their projected high-leverage spots\u2014particularly for **Andy Pages**\u2014could trigger a mid-day efficiency drop.",
